LC 881 — Boats to Save People
Pattern:Two Pointers + Greedy

Logic
Sort people.
l = lightest, r = heaviest.
Put the heaviest person in a boat.
If lightest can fit with them → pair them.
Otherwise, heavy person goes alone.

Algorithm
Sort the array.
Check people[l] + people[r].
If <= limit → l++.
Always r-- and boats++.

CODE:
class Solution {
public:
    int numRescueBoats(vector<int>& p, int limit) {
        sort(p.begin(), p.end());
        int l=0, r=p.size()-1, boats=0;
        while (l<=r) {
            if (p[l]+p[r] <= limit) l++;
            r--;
            boats++;
        }
        return boats;
    }
};
EX:
people = [3,2,2,1]
limit = 3

Sort:
[1,2,2,3]

1 + 3 = 4 ❌
→ 3 goes alone

1 + 2 = 3 ✅
→ pair them

2 → alone

Boats = 3 ✅
